			<section id="text-20" class="widget widget_text clearfix"><h3 class="widget-title">News</h3>			<div class="textwidget"></div>
		</section><section id="block-27" class="widget widget_block clearfix"><!--<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://geobon.org/geo-bon-global-conference-monitoring-biodiversity-for-action/" title="GEO BON Global Conference"><img decoding="async" src="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Conference_home_page.jpg" alt="GEO BON Gobal Conference, Monitoring Biodiversity for Action. 10 to 13 October 2023. Montreal, Canada" /></a></figure>
--></section><section id="block-43" class="widget widget_block widget_recent_entries clearfix"><ul class="wp-block-latest-posts__list wp-block-latest-posts"><li><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__featured-image alignleft"><a href="https://geobon.org/new-paper-calls-for-animal-movement-indicators-in-biodiversity-policy/" aria-label="New paper calls for animal movement indicators in biodiversity policy"><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/moveBON_fig_messages-150x150.jpeg" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" style="" srcset="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/moveBON_fig_messages-150x150.jpeg 150w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/moveBON_fig_messages-270x270.jpeg 270w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/moveBON_fig_messages-230x230.jpeg 230w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></a></div><a class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-title" href="https://geobon.org/new-paper-calls-for-animal-movement-indicators-in-biodiversity-policy/">New paper calls for animal movement indicators in biodiversity policy</a><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-excerpt">Move BON is pleased to announce the publication of a new paper in Nature Reviews Biodiversity that highlights the critical role of animal movement in biodiversity monitoring and policy. The paper, A call to integrate animal movement into biodiversity indicators, argues that information on how animals move through landscapes and</div></li>
<li><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__featured-image alignleft"><a href="https://geobon.org/geo-bon-welcomes-samara-manzin-as-a-bon-in-a-box-biodiversity-data-scientist/" aria-label="GEO BON welcomes Samara Manzin as a BON in a Box Biodiversity Data Scientist"><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-150x150.jpeg" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" style="" srcset="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-150x150.jpeg 150w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-300x300.jpeg 300w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-270x270.jpeg 270w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin-230x230.jpeg 230w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Samara-Manzin.jpeg 625w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></a></div><a class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-title" href="https://geobon.org/geo-bon-welcomes-samara-manzin-as-a-bon-in-a-box-biodiversity-data-scientist/">GEO BON welcomes Samara Manzin as a BON in a Box Biodiversity Data Scientist</a><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-excerpt">I am excited to be joining the GEO BON team as the biodiversity data scientist working on the BON in a BOX tool. I recently completed my Master&#8217;s degree at McGill University, where my research focused on predicting large-scale changes in mammal space use in response to intensifying human footprint.</div></li>
<li><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__featured-image alignleft"><a href="https://geobon.org/call-for-expression-of-interest-hosting-the-geo-bon-secretariat/" aria-label="Call for Expression of Interest: Hosting the GEO BON Secretariat"><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" style="" srcset="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-150x150.png 150w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-300x300.png 300w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-270x270.png 270w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-230x230.png 230w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-192x192.png 192w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-180x180.png 180w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon-32x32.png 32w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/cropped-site-icon.png 512w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></a></div><a class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-title" href="https://geobon.org/call-for-expression-of-interest-hosting-the-geo-bon-secretariat/">Call for Expression of Interest: Hosting the GEO BON Secretariat</a><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-excerpt">GEO BON is soliciting offers to host the GEO BON Secretariat The Group on Earth Observations Biodiversity Observation Network (GEO BON) is a global network that connects biodiversity observation initiatives, organizations, and scientists to support coordinated biodiversity monitoring and reporting worldwide. It supports the monitoring of biodiversity change through the</div></li>
<li><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__featured-image alignleft"><a href="https://geobon.org/bon-in-a-box-published-in-bioscience-an-open-and-collaborative-platform-for-biodiversity-monitoring-indicator-calculation-and-reporting/" aria-label="BON in a Box published in BioScience: An Open and Collaborative Platform for Biodiversity Monitoring, Indicator Calculation, and Reporting"><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/BiaB_large-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" style="" srcset="https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/BiaB_large-150x150.png 150w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/BiaB_large-270x270.png 270w, https://geobon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/BiaB_large-230x230.png 230w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></a></div><a class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-title" href="https://geobon.org/bon-in-a-box-published-in-bioscience-an-open-and-collaborative-platform-for-biodiversity-monitoring-indicator-calculation-and-reporting/">BON in a Box published in BioScience: An Open and Collaborative Platform for Biodiversity Monitoring, Indicator Calculation, and Reporting</a><div class="wp-block-latest-posts__post-excerpt">A new paper describing the latest version of BON in a Box has been published in BioScience. The article expands on the motivations, design and potential of BON in a Box as an open and collaborative platform for biodiversity monitoring, indicator calculation and reporting. The Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (GBF)</div></li>
</ul></section><section id="block-34" class="widget widget_block widget_text clearfix">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
</section><section id="custom_html-3" class="widget_text widget widget_custom_html clearfix"><div class="textwidget custom-html-widget"><div ><p style="text-align: right;font-size:12px;margin-top:-20px;position:relative"><a  style="display: block;" title="All news" href="https://geobon.org/all-news/">All news &gt;&gt;</a></p></div></div></section><section id="block-32" class="widget widget_block clearfix"><div class="newsletter-subscribe">

